   "daf": "40b",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ עֶבֶד שֶׁעֲשָׂאוֹ רַבּוֹ אַפּוֹתֵיקֵי וְשִׁיחְרְרוֹ: מִי שִׁחְרְרוֹ? אָמַר רַב: רַבּוֹ רִאשׁוֹן. שׁוּרַת הַדִּין אֵין הָעֶבֶד חַיָּיב כְּלוּם לְרַבּוֹ שֵׁנִי –",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The mishna taught the case of «a slave whose master set him aside as designated repayment» of a debt «to other» people «and» afterward «emancipated him.» The Gemara clarifies: «Who emancipated him? Rav said: His first master» emancipated him, and the mishna is teaching as follows: «According to the letter of the law, the slave is not obligated to» serve «his second master at all.»"
  }
